    {
      "memory_id": "m016",
      "summary": "The user grows old-fashioned heirloom roses from her mother and Knock Outs planted a few years ago for easier care, and finds February pruning advice useful. She is involved in a church choir, planning an Easter program around February while being careful about gatherings due to the past year, with members having mixed comfort levels about in-person meetings. To coordinate choir rehearsals despite unpredictable schedules from grandbabies and doctor's appointments, she aims to organize practices whenever enough voices are available, sometimes on weekends or midweek mornings, and is considering a rolling availability poll; the choir mixes experienced old-timers with newer members who joined last fall, and she wants to balance engagement for both groups, especially when only a small group can attend some weeks, with most members able to handle text messages or simple links though a few are not keen on smartphones.",
